  "description": "share-v1 codes (fed-wire §3.7). byes are the five new bye codes, each as a whole bye frame. errors are the codes a share_result error can carry: the four new ones and the existing ones share calls answer with. frame_hex is that error without never_ran; frame_with_never_ran_hex, present only where never_ran_allowed, carries never_ran true. A never_ran on any other code is a violation (see frames.json). Codes are an open set: a receiver keeps an unknown fed_ code, and treats it as unknown unless it carries never_ran.",
